Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:32:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gpu: retain workers and isolate reset generations

Port the renderer fence isolation from Droid-VM 0f2db62ae885 and
resource ownership fix e7c13165084d (Droid-VM/crosvm pull request 12).
Keep the worker and renderer alive across device reset, release
old mappings and display imports, restore configured scanouts,
and prevent late callbacks from retiring replacement queues.

Vendor the already-locked rutabaga_gfx 0.1.80 library so these
resource-lifetime changes are part of the same source queue.
The dependency version and other Cargo pins remain unchanged.

BUG=None
TEST=ARM64 release build
TEST=Four fence/reset tests, including real worker reactivation
TEST=Resource detach/unref dispatch through its owning component

Purpose: Retain workers and isolate reset generations.
Origin: Droid-VM/crosvm commits cited above.
Upstream-Status: Downstream GunyahVM carry; not submitted to crosvm upstream.
